---
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber off
    actor Operator as Developer or Admin
    participant Loader as Geometry load job<br/>loadGeometriesFromKml (proposed)
    participant KML as Alberta government KML<br/>(same source as website)
    participant DB as Supabase DB<br/>W26_sites-pa, W26_kml_sites
    participant Pages as Map and admin pages
    participant Geo as /api/geocode route
    participant OC as OpenCage API

    Note over Operator,OC: Covers US 6.0.1. W26_sites-pa has no geometry columns today.<br/>"(proposed)" = the step is not in the code today.<br/>Open question: load the KML into a table or read the file each time. W26_kml_sites is the proposed option.

    Operator->>Loader: Start geometry load (proposed)
    Loader->>KML: Download KML file
    KML-->>Loader: Placemarks with boundaries
    Loader->>DB: Store every placemark in W26_kml_sites:<br/>source_feature_id, name, boundary, loaded_at (proposed)
    Loader->>DB: Read active W26_sites-pa rows
    DB-->>Loader: Active sites
    loop Each active site
        Loader->>Loader: Match site name to a placemark
        alt Match is found
            Loader->>DB: Set source_feature_id, boundary as in the KML,<br/>and centre point (lat, lng) on the site (AT 1, AT 2)
        else No match
            Loader->>Loader: Leave source_feature_id NULL (AT 3)
        end
    end
    Loader-->>Operator: Report matched and unmatched counts
    Operator->>Pages: Open unmatched sites list (proposed)
    Pages->>DB: Read active W26_sites-pa rows<br/>where source_feature_id IS NULL
    DB-->>Pages: Unmatched sites (the AT 3 list)
    Pages-->>Operator: Show sites for an Admin to fix

    opt A site has no point and fallback geocoding is used (AT 4)
        Pages->>Geo: GET /api/geocode?q=site name (exists)
        Geo->>OC: Geocode request to the external API
        alt External API returns a result
            OC-->>Geo: lat, lng
            Geo-->>Pages: lat, lng
        else External API refuses the request or its quota is exhausted
            OC-->>Geo: Error or no result
            Geo-->>Pages: No result
        end
    end

    Pages->>DB: Read site boundary and centre point (AT 2)
    DB-->>Pages: Geometry
    Pages-->>Operator: Draw site on the map

    Note over Pages,OC: Decision: fallback geocoding uses the external OpenCage API directly.<br/>There is no application database cache. The OpenCage account quota limits requests.<br/>StewardLog calls OpenCage separately from the phone.
